# Why: Route new external orgs from the default BIZRETHINK claim (overlay 002's
#      route, which gave new orgs full internal-tier access) to the PRO claim
#      with a 14-day trial. On trial expiry, a sweep cron downgrades them to
#      FREE. BizRethink-operated internal orgs get bizrethinkInternal=true
#      flagged separately (admin override or migration) and stay on the
#      BIZRETHINK tier without trial bookkeeping.
#
#      This is SaaS-billing Phase 1: pivot from "every new org gets full
#      features" to "every new org gets PRO features for 14 days, then
#      downgrades to FREE unless they subscribe." Matches the pricing
#      decisions in memory/pacta_usp_and_pricing.md.
#
#      Three call sites — must merge consistently. Drift between any two
#      sites breaks the trial funnel (one site PRO+trial, another FREE).
#
#        1. `packages/lib/server-only/organisation/create-organisation.ts`
#           — `createPersonalOrganisation()`. The base function called by
#           the email-password signup path. Overrides `INTERNAL_CLAIM_ID.PRO`
#           and calls `startTrialForNewOrg({ organisationId, internal: false })`
#           after creation (defensive try/catch — trial record failure
#           doesn't roll back the org).
#
#        2. `packages/trpc/server/organisation-router/create-organisation.ts`
#           — `createOrganisationRoute` mutation. The TRPC route used by
#           the in-app "Create New Organisation" button.
#
#        3. `packages/trpc/server/admin-router/create-admin-organisation.ts`
#           — `createAdminOrganisationRoute` mutation. The admin-panel
#           variant. Identical behaviour but called by an admin acting
#           on behalf of a new tenant.
#
#      Companion files (no patches — new files outside upstream's tree):
#        - packages/bizrethink/server-only/billing/start-trial-for-new-org.ts
#          (writes the trial row + sets trial_ends_at)
#        - packages/bizrethink/server-only/trpc/organisation-billing-router.ts
#          (provides /billing data + trial status to the in-app billing page)
#
# Why-not-additive: The claim assignment happens INLINE in upstream's
#      org-creation flow as a single argument to `createOrganisation()`.
#      There's no extension point. Same for the trial-setup call — it has
#      to happen after the org row exists but before the function returns.
#      Inline patches are unavoidable.
#
# Discipline note — relationship to overlay 002:
#      Overlay 002 (`002-route-org-creation-to-bizrethink-tier.patch`)
#      historically routed new orgs to BIZRETHINK claim. Overlay 041
#      SUPERSEDES 002 for external orgs. The 002 patch should be marked
#      obsolete and removed in post-merge cleanup (Task TBD), OR retained
#      only for internal-org paths. Resolve during the cleanup workstream.
#
# Upstream-merge-fragility: MEDIUM.
#   - Three call sites with structurally similar patches. Upstream's
#     2026-05-15 biome lint reformatted all three (single-line
#     destructures → multi-line). Patch hunks re-anchor against the new
#     formatting; logic preserved.
#   - If upstream renames `INTERNAL_CLAIM_ID.FREE` to `internalClaims.free`
#     (lowercase property access) inconsistently across the three files,
#     the patches need to use whichever accessor each file uses.
#   - If upstream adds new arguments to `createOrganisation()` or its
#     trpc routes, the patches may need to thread the new args through.
